- never use javascript function expression without curly braces () => { return null } instead of () => null
- to conditionally change classes in jsx use the classNames utility from classnames package, don't use ${}
- when using classnames() in jsx, never use the object syntax, always use && or inline if. for example  <div className={classNames('foo', true && 'bar')} /> instead of  <div className={classNames('foo', { bar: true })} /> 
- try to use early returns instead of else branches, using the golang style as an example. Try to minimize code nesting. Instead of using many if else branches use early returns. always choose the if branch with the less amount of code first, this way code nesting will be minimal.